s  including the idea of transhumanism and  what it really means to be human in a  world where people use technology to  essentially turn their bodies into  machines at what point that someone who  replaces their body with mechanical  parts stop being human and  become a machine can someone who goes  full cyborg still be considered human is  there an essence of spirit that makes us  human is there a ghost in the shell that  is the fundamental question and it is a  fascinating one the 1995 animated film  was followed in 2002 by an anime series  called ghost in the shell stand alone  complex in this adaptation the members  of section 9 take on terrorism  cybercrime and government corruption in  the Laughing Man and individual 11  investigations although this series does  not follow directly the events of the  original manga it is still a very  interesting anime with 50 episodes and a  feature-length film so if you're looking  for ghost in the shell content to binge  watch this is definitely a great place  to start as always with ghost in the  shell this series deals with important  philosophical issues from the  relationship between modern technology  and social behavior to artificial  intelligence or AI in 2004 a second  ghost in the shell animated film was  produced as a sort of sequel to the 1995  film best known as ghost in the shell to  innocence this film features the same  characters from the previous film and it  is based on some of the events in the  original manga however it is not  directly connected to the previous film  and it can be considered an independent  story in this film section 9  investigates a series of murders  connected to malfunctioning gynoids or  female sex robots our protagonists to  learn that human consciousness is being  artificially and illegally transferred  into the sex box in order to make them  more realistic and section nine suspects  that this fact is connected to the  reason behind the murders as you can  tell this film also deals with major  philosophical questions about what it  means to be human about human nature and  human sexuality this film was selected  as the best science fiction film at the  2004 nihon SF taisho awards in 2013 a  new adaptation under the name ghost in  the shell arise was launched as an  original video animation or  ova this ova was made up of four  episodes and it ran through mid-2014  then in 2015 it received two additional  episodes and most of the cast that  created arise went on to create another  feature length ghost in the shell film  in 2015 and that film was called ghost  in the shell the new movie the event so  arrives take place in 20 27 which is two  years before the events of the original  1995 film in three years before the  events of the standalone complex anime  however a rise has been officially  termed as a reimagining so that means  that the creator's wanted to stay away  from the continuity of the other series  and wanted to create an independent  story in this sense each adaptation of  ghost in the shell can be seen as an  independent story because although they  all share many common elements none of  them are directly connected to each  other finally an American live-action  adaptation called simply ghost in the  shell is coming out on March 31st 2017  and it stars Scarlett Johansson as the  major and leader of section 9 from what  we can tell right now from the trailer  this movie will revolve around the fact  that the major who has a fully  cybernetic body that she has been using  to fight crime was actually lied to  about her past the major was led to  believe that she lost her family in a  terrorist attack and that her injuries  were so grave that she had to be turned  into a cyborg to save her life however  it is implied that her mind was actually  deliberately tampered with in order to  turn her into a deadly weapon for the  government the new movie will likely  follow the major search for the truth  about her past and it will likely deal  with important political and  philosophical issues while also  featuring a lot of action and I will now  talk a bit about the main characters of  the ghost in the shell franchise who  will also appear in the new film first  we have what oko Kusanagi or the major  who will be played by scarlett johansson  in the live-action adaptation she is the  field commander of Public Security  section 9 and she is known for being  strong in mind and body for being very  intelligent  and for being an expert in hacking and  military tactics then we have bottle the  majors second in command at section nine  and an experience special operative with  a long military career despite his rough  exterior in the ghost in the shell  franchise he is actually known for his  kind heart and good sense of humor then  we have uh Tamaki the chief executive  director of section 9 he is a  no-nonsense leader who is willing to put  his career and reputation on the line to  protect the members of section 9 from  government corruption and political  intrigue and we have tova usually  portrayed as the youngest member of  section 9 and the only one with a family  he is known for having the least  cybernetic modifications done to his  body and for being the most natural tobu  saw was recruited into section 9 because  of his exceptional detective skills  because of his strong sense of right and  wrong and because his lack of cyber 9  nation gives him a different perspective  from the other members and finally we  have kuzyk who is one of the antagonist  in the ghost in the shell stand alone  complex individual 11 arc and who will  be appearing in the new film as the  primary villain in the trailers for the  new movie it is hinted that koozie is an  early form of a full-sized Borg created  by the government before the procedure  was perfected with the major he now  appears to be a criminal who wants to  force the major to face the truth about  her past I just want to give a quick  thank you too sir 